# scripts/opcount: `flattree stats` reads the JSON document of N records
# that `flattree gen -seed 1 -n N` writes into the flat tree and reports on
# it; the cost of one record is the slope between the two sizes. The
# control is the hand Go program of the same layout.
unit record
sizes 20000 160000
input self gen -seed 1 -n {n}
args stats {input}
control cmd/ergo/testdata/flattree/control
